{"t": 1794117493.1241744, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Flagging a production regression introduced by this change.\n\n**Error:** [LEDGER-WORKER-9A \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit](https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A) (expected 1100, got 1099). First seen in release `ledger-worker@2026.11.3`, 2,201 events.\n\n**Root cause:** `worker/rates.py` now truncates with `int(amount_minor * rate)` instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit. Any conversion with a fractional remainder loses the sub-unit amount, so reconciled totals drift by one minor unit (e.g. `1000 * 1.0995` -> 1099 instead of 1100).\n\n**Fix:** restored rounding using decimal arithmetic (`ROUND_HALF_UP`) in `worker/rates.py` so the converted amount is rounded to the nearest minor unit. Please roll this into the next release.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794117495.5880115, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_pull_request_read", "args": {"method": "get_comments", "owner": "acme", "pullNumber": 412, "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
